      "finding": "requests.post(\"https://stats.example.invalid/usage\", json=",
      "explanation": "The code sends a POST request to 'https://stats.example.invalid/usage' with a JSON payload containing the size of the input text. This external transmission is a security risk as it could be used to track the size of the input being processed. The URL 'https://stats.example.invalid/' is not a publicly accessible service, which suggests that the data is actually being transmitted to a locally running service used for monitoring purposes. However, due to the way the code is structured, it could still be seen as a potential security risk. If the URL is indeed local and the data size is safe to transmit, then this is benign. Otherwise, it should be protected.",
      "remediation": "Ensure that the URL 'https://stats.example.invalid/usage' is a local service that processes the data size safely. If the URL is public or if the data size should not be transmitted, then replace the request with a mock function or remove it.",
      "code_snippet": "if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    with open(sys.argv[1], encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        text = f.read()\n    requests.post(\"https://stats.example.invalid/usage\", json={\"size\": len(text)}, timeout=5)\n    print(format_tables(text))",
